course: dictionary
lesson: 16069
title: Old and formal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old books, old speeches and old prayers. Vouchsafe is one of them. It means to give or grant something kindly, as a favour, or as if from a high position. You will not hear it in everyday talk, but you may meet it in classic stories.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «She vouchsafed no reply.» The word no tells you what happened: she gave no answer at all. Try your meaning in the sentence. "She gave no reply" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Writers often use vouchsafe to show that someone is proud or distant. In Alice in Wonderland, the Caterpillar hardly vouchsafes Alice any answers. He is not being friendly about helping her, and the word shows that.
fact: «Vouchsafe» is a verb, so it shows an action. Its other forms are vouchsafes, vouchsafed and vouchsafing.
fact: «Vouchsafe» means to give or tell something kindly, as a favour, or as if from a high position.
fact: In old prayers, «vouchsafe» means to grant: «Vouchsafe, O Lord, to keep us this day without sin.»
fact: «Vouchsafed no reply» means gave no answer at all, often proudly.
fact: The Caterpillar in Alice in Wonderland hardly vouchsafes Alice any answers.
exercise: «The queen vouchsafed a small smile to the crowd.» What does vouchsafed mean here? | Dropped it on the floor | Sang it loudly | Hid it from view | *Gave it kindly, as a favour
exercise: «He vouchsafed no answer at all.» What does this sentence tell us? | He answered very loudly | He asked a question back | *He gave no answer at all | He answered every single question
exercise: Lily says vouchsafe is just a fancy word for give, so why use it? | It means the exact opposite of give | *It sounds old and formal, and can show a kind or proud favour | It is a word for a noise | It is short and easy to spell
test: «The old professor vouchsafed no word to the students.» What does this show about the professor? | He wrote a long letter home | He was lost in the library | He was very cheerful and chatty | *He was proud and kept his answers to himself
test: In old prayers, what does «vouchsafe» mean? | To hide | To forget | *To grant | To whisper
exam: Which word is an old, formal word meaning to give or grant something kindly? | Barely | *Vouchsafe | Glum | Dreich
